From 09668b51f2ea431bb5bca2356b10db0aeb04f82b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: scaraven <nschleicher37@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:35:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] INTERIM S2/S3: allowlist and olean manifest with
 CompPoly's BF64/Ext3 closure
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

scripts/org-closure.sh generates the import allowlist (gate rule 6) and the olean manifest
(rule 5, harness stage 0) of a clean organiser build. The roots are v2's (Mathlib, Contract,
Library, Controls) plus CompPoly.Fields.Binary.BF64 and its submodules Basic, Bytes, Ext3,
Impl, Reduce and BaseCertificate, which DESIGN-v3 §7.4 (V3-9) and AGENTS.md §10 admit for
entries. CompPoly's modules are then pinned by hash, so the gate reports CompPoly's @[csimp]
lemma instead of rejecting it.

scripts/import-allowlist.txt (10 808 modules) and scripts/olean-manifest.sha256 (34 392
entries) are the files generated from a clean setup-scratch.sh org build of this branch
(manifest paths: that build). Stage S3 replaces all three.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
